{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1540442-warped-dominion-the-carp-hosts-and-the-river-tyrant","id":1540442,"title":"Warped Dominion: The Carp Hosts and the River Tyrant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-15T11:03:42-07:00","id":1540442,"title":"Warped Dominion: The Carp Hosts and the River Tyrant","content":"My irrational and personal hatred of the Pacific Northwest's invasive goldfish has manifested in the form of a Host. I've posted this in a few discords already, and I figured this was as good a time as any to try posting them on the forums. Let me know what people think, I'm quite happy with how these turned out and I'd love some feedback.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>THE RIVER TYRANT</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The throne room drowns in silt and sand, choked by the river\u2019s upturned muck. Throngs of petitioners prostrate themselves before it, sinking hands and knees and inhuman appendages into shifting soil. The barest hints of serpentine coils break through hazy air and hazier Gauntlet, revealing the monster lairing in its depths. A blurred outline churns through the antechamber\u2019s rotting mud, only visible through brief flashes of golden, wriggling scales. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The River Tyrant, unbound semi-god of the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, holds court. All rise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meninna lorekeepers hoard sightings of the beast across time and space, plucking pearls of wisdom from disparate, cataclysmic encounters. A many-finned monster systematically destroying sacred sites along the length of the Mississippi, eradicating their guardian packs and lodges. A war prosecuted against the spirit nobles of the Yangtze during the Spring and Autumn period, a squirming dragon leading hordes of Magath into battle against massed armies of spirits and Uratha. Its week-long fight with one of Black Wolf\u2019s Royal Avatars over the Nile, which ended with a wolf-headed shadow broken in half, the area\u2019s Hunters in Darkness scattered to the four winds, and the River Tyrant nowhere to be seen. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each disaster heralds a new discovery. It appears primarily around rivers and port cities, but always when the Carp Hosts are deeply entrenched and heavily endangered. It acts as a guardian spirit, seeking and eradicating the greatest threats to the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu\u2019s </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">survival with overwhelming force. If that fails, then it uses finesse, leveraging armies and retainers with the grace of a natural-born commander. Once the danger has passed, the River Tyrant vanishes, breaking apart into shimmering water and iridescent scales. The Carp Host population plummets in its wake, even as mortal loyalists and Magath retainers find squirming shardlets, kept in secret until the next patriarchs can emerge once more. Unfortunately, there\u2019s more than one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hunters in Darkness have a theory.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once in a blue moon, when the Carp choke the rivers and the Hosts choke the Gauntlet, the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">start to swim. Their wretched patriarchs, bloated shards that rule over courts of hybrids and lesser \u2018princelings\u2019 put aside old grudges and older hungers to join together, streams feeding into the same river. Ancient alchemies create a fraction of a fraction of the Tyrant River, a wriggling dragon with fish for scales, a composite of hundreds of hundreds of shards that holds itself together just long enough to perform the task it was created for. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the River Tyrant shatters - it always does - the Carp Hosts go with it. Small mercies. The shards, however, survive. They\u2019re diminished, scattered, but very much alive. They wait, they scheme, they grow, all certain that </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>next</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> time, the Joining will be a success. Next time, they\u2019ll reign forever.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Kukulugalu</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Carp Hosts, or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, are children of the Tyrant River, the god that claimed ownership over Spirit and Flesh alike in the days of Pangaea. Inside each bloated carp that wriggles through the Gauntlet\u2019s mud is the blood of a dragon, and each one of them knows it. They\u2019re so close to seizing his throne. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">form a middle ground between the solipsistic monsters of the Azlu and the hysterical Beshilu collective, organizing themselves into squabbling family units. The least of their number are distended goldfish barely the size of a thumb, soft to the touch as they writhe just below the skin of their \u2018parent\u2019. These older hosts carefully cultivate broods of lesser shards that swim between leathery skin and desiccated muscle. Once a body is chosen or an example needs to be made, these Hosts\u2019 scaled fingers stab into their unlucky victim, skin bursting apart as ambitious shardlets seek to claim their first piece of territory. Only one canny </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">will succeed, of course, but the corpses of their siblings serve as a good first meal for the bloodline\u2019s newest son.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bodies that have Carp Hosts swimming through their skin quickly thicken and leather as the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">grows larger within their body. This natural armor rapidly ages the corpse, leaving them hunched and wizened. Unlike other Hosts, the Carp don\u2019t need to consume other shards to continue their evolution, using potent essence alchemies to grow larger and stronger. To be considered a patriarch, a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> must have mastered the secret of fermenting its own essence; an art that goes hand in hand with spawning new shards. At this stage, the only way they can grow farther is by consuming others of their kind; no the mewling princelings or bestial hybrids, but other patriarchs. It\u2019s much harder than it sounds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These bloated old Shartha are petty kings of fetid kingdoms, polluting their territories\u2019 Gauntlets with self-indulgent squirming. Decrepit husks disgorge bloated Carp into the Gauntlet, their passing stirring up spiritual silt that chokes the senses and homogenizes essence. These irresistible globs of piscine ephemera are poisoned chalices for the spirits that consume them; eat too much and find yourself forever changed. Every sort of Magath imaginable makes its home in a Carp Host\u2019s kingdom, courtiers and generals that can\u2019t help but serve.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Carp Dynasty\u2019s Flesh-side assets are far weaker, limited to newly-Joined hosts that govern sections of their patriarch\u2019s territory and a few bestial hybrids that lurk in the rivers and the Gauntlet. Unlike other Shartha, the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> see hybridization as an indignity, not apotheosis. Melding with human corpses prevents a Carp Host from properly polluting the Gauntlet, from creating its own kingdom and its own brood of servant-children, from running with their fellows to conjure a River Tyrant. Hybrids are few and far between, and while they may be powerful, they\u2019re still slaved to their Patriarch\u2019s orders. For their own parts, the Patriarchs treat hybrids like potent weapons, husbanded and hidden until they need to be unleashed. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ultimately, Magath and hybrids serve the same purpose. Like other Shartha, the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">consume each other. Unlike other Hosts, each one knows </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>exactly</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> what the boundaries of every other Carp\u2019s territory are. Armies are raised, schemes are hatched, and assassins are made, all towards the same ends; annihilation and consumption. Carp Host dynasties twist the Hisil into a warzone. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The River Tyrant is a reflection of one of the Old Gods of Pangea: faceted, multifarious, and utterly inhuman. Like everything produced by the Shartha, it\u2019s a mockery - a dragon made wrong. Filmy fins protrude from its body at odd angles, crusted with river muck and roiling essence. Rows upon rows of dull scales slide across its serpentine bodies and malformed claws, coiling and writhing almost independently. Close inspection shows the truth, pairs of eyes protruding from each misshapen scale that gaze out at the world with callous arrogance. Each scale is its own </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, a bloated Carp half-fused with its fellows but still with its own malign intelligence. Every so often, the light hits one just right, and it glows a brilliant, gleaming gold. If the Uratha were to pierce its armor, stabbing through hardened Shartha and coiling essence, they\u2019d find nothing beneath. The River Tyrant is hollow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tyrant\u2019s head, lacking the horns or frills of a dragon, reveals its true origins. Twin soft nubs, filled with some viscous white substance, protrude from an elongated piscine head. Its twisted, distended jawbone juts out in a monstrous underbite, rows of razor-sharp teeth pushed out from a mouth that was never designed to bite. The River Tyrant\u2019s fleshy skin tears when it does so anyways, knitting together to force its jaws closed again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When it deigns to speak, the River Tyrant\u2019s voice echoes from a thousand muffled, gurgling throats. It gives ultimatums, makes statements of fact, pronounces doom with cold, detached glee. It neither bargains nor begs with the Uratha. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike other Shartha, even the Carp Hosts, the River Tyrant doesn\u2019t fear Wolf\u2019s children. It believes itself to be a higher class of being, as far above Uratha as the werewolves are above the least of its lesser kin. The Tyrant carries itself with the bearing of a spirit noble even when forced out of its Gauntlet lair, standing and fighting long past when the most arrogant Hosts would flee. It takes any opportunity it can to break its foes, exploding out of the Gauntlet and using corded claws, legions of Magath, and its own monstrous bulk to annihilate them. The River Tyrant does its best to leave a survivor, to spread the word and tell the stories. It adores being feared. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secrets</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hunters in Darkness believe that River Tyrants are born from the collective wills of the area\u2019s Carp Hosts and die once their purpose is fulfilled. These guardian gods are thought to be an unfortunately deadly stage in the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu\u2019s </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">life cycle, dying and being reborn as hundreds of squirming carp. Technically, they\u2019re even right. What the Uratha fail to realize is that the malign intelligence gleaming in the River Tyrant\u2019s squamous eyes is the same spark every time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever the Carp Hosts\u2019 instincts compel them to choke the river with bloated shards, running fast and thick in Gauntlet and Flesh, they call out to the primordial depths. The Tyrant River\u2019s bloated carcass rotted away in the Bordermarch\u2019s silt long ago, but a god\u2019s ambition doesn\u2019t die so easily. The </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu\u2019s </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">desperation grants that desire for domination a brief moment of lucidity. It inhabits the hollow dragon they create as it fulfills their most fervent desires, a parody of a Claimed that fits together too well to be one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The River Tyrant remembers Pangea. It remembers ruling large swathes of the Bordermarches, an unbound God over Flesh and Shadow. It remembers Wolf\u2019s jaws around its neck. It remembers its past incarnations, all of them. It\u2019s beginning to scheme. The River Tyrant is the lingering shade of a Pangean\u2019s desire to rule the worlds, and every time it\u2019s summoned back into the Flesh, it leaves orders when it dies. Servants and Magath are instructed to migrate, to hide, to husband the newest generation of patriarchs around the world\u2019s rivers. Shards are implanted with new suggestions: move, cannibalize, fight for the same territory. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hunters in Darkness have noted a disturbing trend in recent decades: the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are converging. This is by design. Eventually, decades or centuries in the future, the Carp Hosts will find themselves around the same river, carving up Flesh and Shadow alike into petty, feuding dominions. Eventually, they\u2019ll be threatened by something. A massive protectorate, a nation\u2019s government, the concentrated attention of a God of the Shadow. Then, when the Carp choke the river and the Hosts choke the Gauntlet, the River Tyrant will incarnate once more. This time it won\u2019t be hollow. This time, it will live forever. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In its few free moments, the River Tyrant idly hopes that the river that hosts its glorious rebirth will be the Yangtze. There\u2019d be a nice poetry to that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rumors</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>There\u2019s stories of a forum buried deep in a sea of dead links and abandoned domains, one that has all sorts of info, conspiracy theories and manifestos. They say you can only access it if you\u2019ve got info of your own to share. Weirdest fucking thing though, those stories that people say get you past the first page? They\u2019re all about dragons.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The River Tyrant leaves survivors to tell stories and spread fear. When those survivors are human, they start searching for answers. Hunter cells grow in the Tyrant\u2019s wake, ancient orders and tight-knit clans that persist through generations. One shell-shocked teenager went to the forums for answers in 2009, and these cells began to find each other. Nezha.com is small but focused, shrouded behind layers of masterful cybersecurity and half-decent wards. Members compare stories and track records, slowly putting the pieces together. They think they can predict where it\u2019ll show up next. When it wakes up, they\u2019ll be ready.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>I saw something last time we reached into the Hisil. Some big fucking </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">thing</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>, all fins and scales and teeth, rooting around in the mud. Same shit as normal, yeah? But our Hunter in Darkness swears on Black Wolf that it was a Host. Don\u2019t know if she\u2019s right, and I don\u2019t really want to find out. The bite marks on our Rahu means that we don\u2019t have much of a choice.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The largest Carp Host hybrids, piscine monstrosities that barely resemble humanity, spend more time in the Shadow than the Flesh. Here, they tend to courts of Magath and scour the Hisil for unknown ends, waiting for their patriarchs to call them back into the Flesh. Their lairs are potent crucibles of varied streams of essence and all sorts of rare treasures of the Deep Shadow. Any pack that could get past such a hybrid\u2019s defenses would find themselves rich beyond imagining.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>You see the new tower in the Hisil? Yeah, the one with all those scales. Our totem can\u2019t keep itself away from the damned thing, keeps on demanding that we \u2018crack the secrets\u2019 and \u2018reveal the bounty within\u2019. Only reason we haven\u2019t tried yet is that the Eightbound got to it first, and their totem\u2019s an </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ensah.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Carp Hosts stir up the Gauntlet, sometimes the homogenized Essence they create congeals into scaled structures in the Hisil. These structures are irresistible to spirits, who can feel the bounty of Essence within but can\u2019t see that it\u2019s Magath in nature, and the Hisil around these areas quickly becomes a warzone. The victor, bloodied and broken, cracks the tower open and greedily devours its prize. The resulting Magath quickly becomes one of the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu\u2019s</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> most powerful servants.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Story Hooks</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The city's Hisil is in disarray. A </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">hybrid has gone rogue, gorging itself on the dynasty that once shackled it. It has grown far beyond its masters\u2019 reckoning, a scheming, slavering dragon-beast tearing its way through the Carp Hosts\u2019 carefully balanced dominions. The remaining Patriarchs are terrified of what this abomination represents, and their ironclad grips are starting to slip.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A set of Carp Host Dynasties have moved into the area, one after another. These patriarchs know that they\u2019re uniquely vulnerable without their normal networks of servants and children, and have been offering to teach the local power players the secrets of essence alchemy in exchange for their aid in killing the other patriarchs. At least one of them has approached the Ivory Claws.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are on the back foot, harried and pushed back to the edge of the river bank. Days before the city\u2019s protectorate\u2019s final assault on their holdings is set to occur, a horrific Magath approaches the pack, informing them that the Carp Hosts are planning to conjure a River Tyrant. It offers to guide the pack to where the ritual is being performed, so long as they can save it from eternity as an abomination.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Statline</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The River Tyrant</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>: </b>Intelligence 6, Wits 4, Resolve 5; Strength</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 15, Dexterity 7, Stamina 10; Presence 8, Manipulation 3, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Composure 4</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skills:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animal Ken 2, Athletics 4, Brawl 5, Empathy 2, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intimidation 5, Occult 4, Politics 3, Stealth 2, Subterfuge 1, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Survival 3</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Air of Menace, Eidetic Memory, Iron Stamina 3, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Relentless, Small Unit Tactics</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 9</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">50</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">35</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 11</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 9</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">25</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 22</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Armored Hide 3, Destructive Aura 2, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Discorporate, Dread Presence*, Essence Fermentation*, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Flight, Gauntlet Churn* Gauntlet Cloak, Honorary Rank 5*, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monstrous Resilience, Natural Weapons 3, Stir Gauntlet*,</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Surprise Entrance, Swift, Taint, Tyrannic Echoes</span></span>*</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>DREAD PRESENCE</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The creature is an ancient monster with a potent legend, one that grows fat off of the fear of its lessers. It gains +2 to rolls against creatures with the Shaken or Spooked conditions. Once per target per round, it can spend 1 Essence to trigger the effects of these conditions without resolving them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>ESSENCE FERMENTATION (KUKULUGALU ONLY)</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Powerful Carp Hosts can manipulate their own internal alchemy, turning their Essence reserves into a roiling cauldron that bubbles endlessly. The </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> may take 1 bashing damage to regain 2 Essence at the start of its turn. In addition, it may spend a point of Essence to boost an attribute by 1 for a single roll, up to a +3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>GAUNTLET CHURN (KUKULUGALU ONLY)</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By spending an hour in a meditative trance, costing 1 Essence in the process, a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> can churn 10 square yards of the Gauntlet into an opaque morass that scrambles Essence flows and chokes visibility. Characters take a -3 penalty to perceiving across the affected area as ethereal silt and muck chokes their senses. In addition, Churned Gauntlets are perilous to travel across; characters must spend a point of essence or be transported to a random location within the affected area. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence produced within the affected area is blended and homogenized, spat out of the Gauntlet as a mix of conflicting resonances. Beings that consume this blended Essence are naturally more inclined towards the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kukulugalu,</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> increasing their impression level to the Carp by 1 for every X points of Essence they consume, where X is their Rank or Honorary Rank. In addition, spirits that eat this Essence gain the Addicted (Blended Essence) Condition until the end of the Chapter. If they become Magath by eating this Essence, the Condition becomes Persistent.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>HONORARY RANK</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The creature is a potent being in the Ephemeral Realms, even if it isn't an ephemeral itself. It counts as having a spirit rank equal to this Dread Power's rating whenever it would benefit from doing so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>TYRANNIC ECHOES (RIVER TYRANT ONLY)</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever a creature within the same scene as the River Tyrant takes an action to dominate, assert authority over, or subjugate someone else, the River Tyrant can spend 1 Essence to give that action the rote quality. If the action succeeds, the River Tyrant regains all its Willpower and all other parties involved gain the Leveraged (River Tyrant) condition.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28575-kaboomatic","name":"Kaboomatic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:10:42-07:00","id":1540448,"title":"","content":"fuck yeah! Evil fish!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:18:25-07:00","id":1540450,"title":"","content":"I fear these things, these river basturds<br /> <br /> Well done.<br /> <br /> I wonder how they veiw the other Hosts if they are the kings of the shards","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:25:46-07:00","id":1540454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1540442-warped-dominion-the-carp-hosts-and-the-river-tyrant?p=1540450#post1540450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder how they veiw the other Hosts if they are the kings of the shards</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not so much the kings of other shards as they are shards that naturally organize themselves into kingdoms. They treat other shards like rival/enemy nations as well, viewing Lamprey cults, Beshilu collectives, and solo Azlu - along with the various other equivalent units of shartha - as organizations to be used against their rivals but eventually exterminated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28575-kaboomatic","name":"Kaboomatic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T14:51:35-07:00","id":1540473,"title":"","content":"Okay, this was a very pleasant surprise! It\u2019s been quite a long time since anyone has posted a new type of Shartha, and it\u2019s always a joy to see a persons creativity at work doing it. Aquatic Hosts in general are super interesting, so this one tickles my fancy even more.<br /> <br /> I could see my Ant Hosts giving these things a side eye, before getting the spears ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T16:07:42-07:00","id":1540476,"title":"","content":"A true terror lurking in murky waters, the River Tyrant is either a natural disaster that must be avoided at all costs or high octane fight with its own spotlight in the chronicle. Meanwhile, the carp host lend themselves to all sorts of horror scenarios. Its just an great antogonist overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T17:50:04-07:00","id":1540482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1540442-warped-dominion-the-carp-hosts-and-the-river-tyrant?p=1540476#post1540476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A true terror lurking in murky waters, the River Tyrant is either a natural disaster that must be avoided at all costs or high octane fight with its own spotlight in the chronicle. Meanwhile, the carp host lend themselves to all sorts of horror scenarios. Its just an great antogonist overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! This was a real labor of loathing for me, I've seen firsthand the damage that goldfish and invasive carp do to my home region's waterways, so I'm glad I got across the horror potential inherent in these squirming dragonspawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28575-kaboomatic","name":"Kaboomatic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:01:53-07:00","id":1540484,"title":"","content":"I'm just asking out of curiosity (SWEAR I'm not nitpicking), but are carp fairly associated with plague or other forms of bad omens? I just mean mythological connections. I'm only asking because it's a common but not always present pattern","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:29:41-07:00","id":1540490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1540442-warped-dominion-the-carp-hosts-and-the-river-tyrant?p=1540484#post1540484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just asking out of curiosity (SWEAR I'm not nitpicking), but are carp fairly associated with plague or other forms of bad omens? I just mean mythological connections. I'm only asking because it's a common but not always present pattern</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK not, this is a fairly recent (but serious) development.<br /> <br /> But carps are associated with dragons, and a lot can be derived from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T19:22:53-07:00","id":1540493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1540442-warped-dominion-the-carp-hosts-and-the-river-tyrant?p=1540484#post1540484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just asking out of curiosity (SWEAR I'm not nitpicking), but are carp fairly associated with plague or other forms of bad omens? I just mean mythological connections. I'm only asking because it's a common but not always present pattern</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not actually sure. Most of my inspiration for carp in this write-up comes from the way they contribute to ecological issues - namely by consuming all the available food in the area while being too big to be eaten themselves and choking up rivers and streams with the muck they stir up from the riverbed. That, plus their associations with dragons, created the blueprint for these guys in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28575-kaboomatic","name":"Kaboomatic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}